Or at least be a possibility of doing something bad.  Or good (by
removing an intrinsic you don't want).  There are lots of cursed-or-
otherwise-obviously-bad things that get used quite a bit (cursed
?oEnchantFoo, unholy water, !oConfusion)

If you've got a bunch of intrinsics, getting rid of aggro or tportitis
could be done easily with a cursed unihorn... at the risk of having to
strip away other intrinsics on the way.

Guaranteed removal of bad thing at the cost of (probably) several good
things is probably reasonably balanced.  People have been known to dance
with gremlins for this purpose.

OTOH, gremlins generally show up later game.  Cursed unihorns are pretty
easy to come by, even in the early game (I know lots of my bones files
produce them, and doesn't unholy water curse a unihorn same as usual?).

Hmm... what if unihorn BUC was based on relative alignment, and --
because of their inherent power and purity of alignment -- cannot be
changed?  For a lawful character, a white unihorn would be cursed
(profiting from the death of a white uni!  *bad*), a grey unihorn would
be uncursed, and a black unihorn would be blessed.

Perhaps only initial BUC should be set that way[1], based on who killed
it.  That is, if you're lawful and kill a white unicorn, that unihorn is
forever cursed, even if you find it in a bones file when playing a
chaotic.  Or if your nalfeshnee pet[2] chews up a black unicorn, that
unihorn is cursed, even if you're lawful.

It's not like unicorns are hard to find.  If you tie the BUC to the
relative alignment and don't let it change, it means that getting a
cursed unihorn with its nifty intrinsic removal has other repercussions
as well.

